--- 3. re-calibrate on all days so far
# Calibration report (2026-09-24)

1341 rows, 354 tokens, 2 day(s) (2026-09-22 to 2026-09-24). Target: cost of selling immediately across all measured venues, vs consolidated mid. 5-fold CV grouped by token.
1097 more sales could not be absorbed by the merged book at all (no venue truncated). They can't be fitted, so they're scored instead: 'false comfort' = share a model prices under 10%. Dropped: 238 sales where a venue capped its levels (thin vs truncated unknowable); 0 token-days with no CMC volume/sigma.

| model | Y | delta | median abs err | median factor off | R^2 (log) | false comfort |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| textbook sqrt, global Y **(shipped)** | 1.91 | 0.500 | 14.7 bps | x1.82 | 0.440 | 81% |
| power law, global Y | 8.59 | 0.720 | 16.1 bps | x1.78 | 0.481 | 44% |
| learned Y per token | per token | 0.720 | 15.5 bps | x1.74 | 0.554 | 46% |

Median absolute error by order size (out-of-fold, bps):

| size | n | sqrt | power | learned |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| $10,000 | 600 | 8.9 | 7.9 | 7.4 |
| $100,000 | 530 | 24.5 | 32.7 | 28.5 |
| $1,000,000 | 170 | 25.9 | 28.8 | 33.2 |
| $10,000,000 | 41 | 87.1 | 96.7 | 116.1 |

What predicts a token's Y (GBM feature importance): log_sigma 0.48, history_days 0.19, log_mcap 0.12, log_volume 0.11, turnover 0.11

The learned model did not beat the power law by the required 5%, so the power law ships. Published as a negative result.

Wrote ingest/calibration.json (used by impact.py) and data/calibration_report.md (for METHODOLOGY.md).
